---
import Component from "../../layouts/Component.astro"
import Anatomy from "../../components/Anatomy.astro"
import AutoExample from "../../components/AutoExample.astro"
import Conditional from "../../components/Conditional.astro"
import DocLink from "../../components/DocLink.astro"
import PropOrClass from "../../components/PropOrClass.astro"
import Usage from "./partials/Usage.astro"
import {
  Avatar as UIAvatar,
  Message as UIMessage,
  Messages as UIMessages,
  ToggleButton as UIToggleButton,
  ToggleGroup as UIToggleGroup,
} from "opui-css/astro"

import AvatarCSS from "@opui/css/components/avatar.css?raw"
import MessageCSS from "@opui/css/components/message.css?raw"

import messageApi from "../../component-api/message/api"
import messagesApi from "../../component-api/messages/api"

export const description =
  "Chat bubbles that group by sender, with attachments, reactions and a typing indicator."

export const keywords = ["chat", "chat bubble", "conversation"]
---

<Component
  description={description}
  slug="message"
  heroAnatomy
  apis={[
    { title: "Messages API", api: messagesApi },
    { title: "Message API", api: messageApi },
  ]}
  browserSupport={[
    "color-mix",
    "container-queries",
    "container-style-queries",
    "corner-shape",
    "has",
    "lh",
  ]}
  changelogPaths={[
    { path: "packages/opui/components/Message", type: "component" },
    { path: "src/docs/components/message.astro", type: "docs" },
    { path: "src/component-examples/message", type: "docs" },
    { path: "packages/opui/css/components/message.css", type: "css" },
    { path: "src/component-api/message", type: "api" },
    { path: "src/component-api/messages", type: "api" },
  ]}
  installationTabs={[
    { title: "message.css", code: MessageCSS, lang: "css" },
    { title: "avatar.css", code: AvatarCSS, lang: "css", isDependency: true },
  ]}
  seeAlsoLinks={[
    { name: "Avatar", href: "/components/avatar" },
    { name: "Toggle", href: "/components/toggle" },
  ]}
>
  <Fragment slot="title">Message</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="preamble">
    Chat bubbles for a conversation. Consecutive messages from the same side
    group into a run, with tighter corners on the avatar side, the author on the
    first message and the <DocLink href="/components/avatar">Avatar</DocLink> on the
    last. For a note from the app, use a <DocLink href="/components/callout"
      >Callout</DocLink
    >.
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="anatomy">
    <Anatomy>
      <UIMessages aria-label="Messages with Saga" style="inline-size: 22rem">
        <UIMessage author="Saga" datetime="2026-10-08T14:31" time="14:31">
          <UIAvatar aria-label="Saga Nyström" role="img" slot="start"
            >SN</UIAvatar
          >
          <p>Here's the current draft.</p>
          <Fragment slot="end">Read</Fragment>
          <UIToggleGroup
            aria-label="Reactions"
            multiple
            name="reaction"
            slot="bottom"
          >
            <UIToggleButton aria-label="Thumbs up, 2" checked value="+1"
              ><span aria-hidden="true">👍 2</span></UIToggleButton
            >
          </UIToggleGroup>
        </UIMessage>
      </UIMessages>
    </Anatomy>
  </Fragment>

  <Usage slot="usage">
    <li slot="when">
      A conversation between people, like support chat or direct messages, in a
      list of <a href="#basics">messages</a>.
    </li>
    <li slot="when">
      A channel with several senders, like a team chat, with a <a
        href="#group-chat">new author</a
      > marking each change of sender.
    </li>
    <li slot="when-not">
      A note from the app, like a warning or a success. Use a <DocLink
        href="/components/callout">Callout</DocLink
      >.
    </li>
    <li slot="when-not">
      Comments on a post, which are read in order rather than as a chat. Use a <DocLink
        href="/components/list">List</DocLink
      >.
    </li>
  </Usage>

  <section id="basics">
    <h2>Basics</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Each message is an <code>li.ui-message</code> in an <code
          >ol.ui-messages</code
        >. Add <code>.ui-outgoing</code> to the messages you sent, put the sender
        in <code>p.ui-header</code>, the text in <code>.ui-content</code>
        and the time in <code>p.ui-footer</code>.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="components"
        >Put each <code>Message</code> in <code>Messages</code>. Set <code
          >outgoing</code
        > on the messages you sent, <code>author</code> and <code>time</code> on every
        message, and the sender's <code>Avatar</code> in the <code>start</code> slot.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="react"
        >Put each <code>Message</code> in <code>Messages</code>. Set <code
          >outgoing</code
        > on the messages you sent, <code>author</code> and <code>time</code> on every
        message, and the sender's <code>Avatar</code> in the <code>start</code> prop.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >Put each <code>Message</code> in <code>Messages</code>. Set <code
          >outgoing</code
        > on the messages you sent, <code>author</code> and <code>time</code> on every
        message, and the sender's <code>Avatar</code> in the <code>start</code> snippet.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <p>
      Bubbles are at most 85% as wide as the list. The author of an outgoing
      message, and of every message in a run but the first, is visually hidden
      and still read by screen readers.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Basics" />
  </section>

  <section id="group-chat">
    <h2>Group chat</h2>
    <p>
      CSS can't compare authors, so mark the first message after the sender
      changes with <PropOrClass prop="newAuthor" class=".ui-new-author" />. Any
      other <code>li</code> between messages, such as a date <DocLink
        href="/components/divider">Divider</DocLink
      >, also starts a new run.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="GroupChat" />
  </section>

  <section id="attachments">
    <h2>Attachments</h2>
    <p>
      A file is an outlined <DocLink href="/components/card">Card</DocLink> in the
      bubble, with an icon, a link and the details in a <DocLink
        href="/components/layout#media">media layout</DocLink
      >.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Attachments" />
  </section>

  <section id="reactions">
    <h2>Reactions</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Put a <DocLink href="/components/toggle">Toggle group</DocLink> of checkboxes
        in <code>.ui-bottom</code>. The label of each input names the emoji and
        the count, and <code>checked</code> marks your own reaction.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="components"
        >Put a <DocLink href="/components/toggle">Toggle group</DocLink> of checkboxes
        in the <code>bottom</code> slot. The label of each toggle names the emoji
        and the count, and <code>checked</code> marks your own reaction.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="react"
        >Put a <DocLink href="/components/toggle">Toggle group</DocLink> of checkboxes
        in the <code>bottom</code> prop. The label of each toggle names the emoji
        and the count, and <code>defaultChecked</code> marks your own reaction.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="svelte"
        >Put a <DocLink href="/components/toggle">Toggle group</DocLink> of checkboxes
        in the <code>bottom</code> snippet. The label of each toggle names the emoji
        and the count, and <code>checked</code> marks your own reaction.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <p>
      The message draws the toggles as separate pills over the bottom edge of
      the bubble, with your own reactions tinted in the primary color. Saving a
      toggle and adding a new emoji are up to you: listen for <code>change</code
      > on the group, and update the count in the label.
    </p>
    <AutoExample name="Reactions" />
  </section>

  <section id="typing">
    <h2>Typing indicator</h2>
    <Conditional as="p">
      <Fragment slot="html"
        >Add <code>.ui-typing</code> to a message to animate three dots in its bubble.
        Give the bubble <code>role="status"</code> and visually hidden text, such
        as "Saga is typing", so screen readers announce it once.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="components"
        >Set <code>typing</code> on a message to animate three dots in its bubble.
        The default slot becomes visually hidden status text, such as "Saga is typing",
        which screen readers announce once.</Fragment
      >
      <Fragment slot="react"
        >Set <code>typing</code> on a message to animate three dots in its bubble.
        The children become visually hidden status text, such as "Saga is typing",
        which screen readers announce once.</Fragment
      >
    </Conditional>
    <p>The dots stand still under reduced motion.</p>
    <AutoExample name="Typing" />
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="accessibility">
    <p>
      The conversation is an <code>ol</code>, named with <code>aria-label</code
      >, so a screen reader announces the number of messages and reads them in
      order. The author is in every bubble, hidden visually where the run makes
      it clear, so each message is read with its sender. Put the time in a <code
        >time</code
      > element with <code>datetime</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      Color alone never carries meaning: an outgoing message is also at the end
      of the list, with "You" as its author. In forced colors mode the bubbles
      get a border and the typing dots stay visible.
    </p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="under-the-hood">
    <p>
      <code>li.ui-message</code> is a grid with a <code>start</code> area for the
      avatar, a <code>content</code> area for the bubble and a <code
        >bottom</code
      > area under it, pulled up by a negative margin so the reactions sit on the
      bubble's edge. A ring in the page's surface color around each pill keeps it
      apart from the bubble. <code>.ui-outgoing</code> swaps the columns and aligns
      the message to the end.
    </p>
    <p>
      A run is found with <code>:has()</code>: a message followed by one on the
      same side tightens its bottom corner on the avatar side and hides its
      avatar, and a message after one on the same side tightens its top corner
      and hides its author. <code>.ui-new-author</code> and any other <code
        >li</code
      > break the chain.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</Component>
